{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall remember all the way.</b> If your inclination says to you to desire silver and gold — place your trust in your Maker <b>and remember all the way that He led you</b>, and you did not need silver or gold." "<b>In the wilderness.</b> This is the great and awesome wilderness that begins at Etham and reaches as far as the land of Moab." "<b>In order to afflict you.</b> To test you whether you will complain." "<b>Whether you would keep His commandments or not.</b> There is no testing with HaShem, for all is revealed before Him; rather, He tested him before the attribute of justice and the attribute of mercy, as he explained in the perasha of Beshalach."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:06.656157127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}